# Recipe: a fillable form

Text inputs, a select, radio buttons, check boxes and a signature field that people fill in a PDF
viewer. The examples in the gem: `stationery examples form --source` (every kind of field) and
`stationery examples contract --source` (initials in the footer of every page, signature fields).

```ruby
class ApplicationFormPdf < Stationery::Document
  MUTED = "#6B7280"

  page size: :a4, margin: 48
  default_text size: 9.5
  metadata title: "Membership application", lang: "en"

  def self.preview = new(name: "Astrid Lindqvist")

  def initialize(name: "")
    super()
    @name = name
  end

  def view_template
    text "Membership application", size: 20, weight: :bold, heading: 1
    spacer 16
    row(gap: 12) do
      labelled("Full name") { text_field "applicant.name", value: @name, required: true }
      labelled("Email") { text_field "applicant.email" }
    end
    spacer 10
    row(gap: 12) do
      column(width: 90) { labelled_field("Postcode") { text_field "applicant.postcode", comb: 5 } }
      labelled("Country") { select "applicant.country", options: %w[Sweden Norway Denmark], value: "Sweden" }
    end
    spacer 10
    labelled_field("Plan") do
      radio "plan", "basic", label: "Basic"
      radio "plan", "pro", label: "Pro", checked: true
    end
    spacer 10
    text_field "notes", multiline: true, height: 60, tooltip: "Anything we should know"
    spacer 10
    checkbox "terms", label: "I accept the terms"
    spacer 24
    signature_field "signature", width: 220, label: "Signature"
  end

  private

  def labelled(label, &) = column { labelled_field(label, &) }

  def labelled_field(label)
    text label, size: 8, color: MUTED
    spacer 3
    yield
  end
end
```

## What matters here

- Fields lay out like boxes (full width by default; `width:` in points), or sit at a page
  position with `at: [x, y]`. They work in rows, boxes and table cells.
- **Dotted names** (`"applicant.name"`) group fields as viewers show them. Radios sharing a name
  are one group whose value is the checked `value`.
- **`select` inside a document is the form field**, not `Kernel#select` or `Enumerable#select`
  called without a receiver: write `list.select { … }` with its receiver.
- **The value of a field is not page text**: `have_pdf_text("Astrid")` does not find it;
  `have_pdf_text("Astrid", fields: true)` does, and `document.fields` after `to_pdf` answers
  `{ "applicant.name" => "Astrid Lindqvist", … }`.
- **`to_png` and `stationery render --png` do not draw form fields**: they are the viewer's widgets,
  so the picture shows the labels and blank space. To see the fields, draw the PDF with MuPDF,
  which paints the appearances the gem writes: `mutool draw -r 96 -o form-%d.png form.pdf`
  (`pdftoppm` draws the values but not the borders). `stationery inspect form.pdf` lists each
  field with its rectangle and value.
- Fields keep PDF/A and PDF/UA (every field has an accessible name from `tooltip:` or its label).
- Signing the file: `sign certificate:, key:, field: "signature"` fills the signature field with
  a digital signature (see [../reference/conformance.md](../reference/conformance.md)).
